    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "HTML Symbol Entities"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Symbols or letters that are not present on your keyboard can be added to HTML using entities."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "To add such symbols to an HTML page, you can use the entity name or the entity number\n(a decimal or a hexadecimal reference) for the symbol:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "html",
      "text": "<p>I will display &euro;</p>\n\n<p>I will display &#8364;</p>\n\n<p>I will display &#x20AC;</p>",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_utf_euro"
    },
